{
  "_comment": [
    "Ground-truth vectors for CAP-4, transcribed from documentation/spelling-diff-spec.md §9.",
    "Deliberately JSON, not TypeScript: this file is the single source of truth for BOTH the",
    "Jest suite and scripts/verify-diff-spec.mjs (which runs the spec's own reference listing).",
    "A .json file is loadable by both without a module resolver, so the two can never drift.",
    "",
    "legacy[]        — 15 vectors CAPTURED FROM THE LIVE PRODUCTION SITE. Ground truth.",
    "                  A failure means compatibility with what users see today is broken.",
    "                  2 of the 15 exercise the exact-match path (exactMatch: true).",
    "transposition[] — 14 vectors of SPECIFIED behaviour, new in v0.2. No production",
    "                  counterpart exists. A failure means the new feature broke, or the",
    "                  tie-break order changed.",
    "structured[]    — §9.4's expected DiffSegment[] for the tricky cases, asserted",
    "                  directly because the structured form is what the UI consumes."
  ],

